    "body": "Reproduced on da340c0f (#1640's head) before the fix: a real P1. Mill-turn bench, B = the #117 r10 punched bar with its r2 cross hole modelled, A = a box x [12, 18] across the drill's line with no hole; r20 bar and 40 x 40 box stocks, aligned and turned a quarter about Z. The part-source cross drill on B generated clean and **posted** on all four stocks. The program sim does not judge the posed chain, and `neighbour_parts` was empty for a cross drill.\n\nfix on issue/1641-cross-drill-neighbours · PR #1644 (stacked on #1640) · pinned by cross_drill_neighbours.rs: a_cross_drill_on_b_into_part_a_is_refused_by_name_on_both_stocks, a_cross_drill_whose_approach_crosses_part_a_is_refused_on_both_stocks, a_neighbours_round_hole_on_the_line_is_not_excused, a_cross_drill_on_b_clear_of_part_a_posts_on_both_stocks, over_mcp_a_part_source_cross_drill_answers_for_the_neighbour_the_same · merges when reviewed\n",
